{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And you shall take no bribe.</b> Even to judge truth, and all the more so in order to pervert justice — for to pervert justice is already stated: ״לֹא תַטֶּה מִשְׁפָּט״ (Deuteronomy 16) (Ketubot 105)." "<b>And blinds the eyes of the discerning.</b> Even one wise in Torah who takes a bribe — in the end his mind will be bereft, he will forget his learning, and the light of his eyes will grow dim (ibid.)." "<b>And perverts.</b> As the Targum renders: וּמְקַלְקֵל — 'and corrupts'." "<b>The words of the righteous.</b> Things that are sifted — true judgments. And so the Targum renders: פִּתְגָמִין תְּרִיצִין — upright words."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:05.729426386Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}